  "definition": "A win is a close in the signalled direction 10 bars after the pattern could first be known — its own close for a candle, four bars later for a double top or head and shoulders, since the final peak is not a swing high until four bars have failed to exceed it. meanFwdAtr is that move in multiples of the 14-bar ATR at the same point, so markets of different volatility can be compared. The measure ignores the path taken, so a move that would have stopped a real trade out on the way still counts as a win — it measures the pattern, not a strategy built on it.",
